      "description": "Watch Elche vs Barcelona highlights and goals from La Liga on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on August 23, 2026. The atmosphere was electric as the two teams met on the pitch, with both sides eager to establish dominance early in the game. It was a matchup that promised tactical intrigue and high-intensity action from the first whistle. Early Pressure and the Opening Goal On August 23, 2026, Barcelona traveled to face Elche in a highly anticipated La Liga clash. The visitors wasted no time in asserting their authority. In the 14th minute, the pressure told when Victor Chust tripped Raphinha inside the penalty area. Raphinha stepped up to take the spot-kick himself, firing a left-footed shot past Matias Dituro to break the deadlock. Just before the halftime whistle, Karim Adeyemi doubled the lead in the 45+3rd minute, finishing clinically after a sequence involving Lamine Yamal and Raphinha . Second Half Dominance and Tactical Masterclass The second half saw Barcelona turn up the heat even further. Following a series of substitutions in the 65th minute, including the introduction of Anthony Gordon and Dani Olmo , the flow of the game shifted decisively. In the 67th minute, Raphinha found the net again for his second goal of the night, set up by Gordon after a brilliant key pass from Olmo . Fermin Lopez then took center stage to put the result beyond any doubt. He scored his first in the 71st minute with a simple tap-in following a pass from Pedri and an assist by Gordon . Fermin Lopez wasn't finished, adding another in the 79th minute with a left-footed strike assisted by Xavi Espart . Despite a late attempt by Elche 's Ezequiel Ponce that forced a save, Barcelona remained in total control, finishing the match with 54% possession and a clean sheet."
